classifier/sources/README.md for provenance.


Sublime Text syntax definitions and themes (via syntect) - MIT / per asset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Syntax highlighting uses the syntect crate (MIT) with its bundled
`default-syntaxes` and `default-themes`. Those definitions originate from
Sublime Text's editor packages and are redistributed through the bat project
(https://github.com/sharkdp/bat); each definition carries its own license,
recorded upstream in syntect's and bat's asset folders. No such asset is
modified here.


Benchmarks
----------
The benchmark suite and its task data live in a separate repository,
https://github.com/chanto-sh/benchmarks, with their own license notices.


Not included
------------
GTFOBins content (GPL-3.0) is deliberately not vendored and no GTFOBins-derived
output is distributed, to keep the classifier data free of copyleft terms. See
classifier/sources/README.md.
